    {
      "id": "2067523072199106807",
      "text": "Claude was NEVER formally accessible in HK btw. This has always been in their terms of service, so this news is all hype.\nPeople in HK and Mainland China have been accessing Claude primarily through VPNs based out of Singapore for the longest time.\nThis is why Singapore smashes records for claude usage.\nHow do i know this? Ive done business travel to China for years as a singaporean, and i ALWAYS use an esim or vpn based on singapore servers to access claude when I’m physically in China.\nThe reason why this has tightened up is because it’s a well-known fact in the industry that chinese model players distill anthropic claude models by buying a fk ton of publicly available claude accnts and training on their responses.\nThis is why Fable 5’s capabilities got copied so quickly.\nAnthropic (and the US govt) know this accelerates\n- commoditization of US AI frontier models\n- security risks if China keeps getting their hands on frontier (to be able to perform cyber attacks, etc)\nAnd are now beginning to tighten controls more via enterprise which is more controllable",
